<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cunimund</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 567</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cunimund was the last king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gepids">Gepids</a>, ruling from about 560 from the region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sirmium">Sirmium</a>. He fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombards</a>, but in 567 the Lombard king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alboin">Alboin</a>, allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avars">Avars</a>, defeated and killed him, ending the Gepid kingdom. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paul-the-deacon">Paul the Deacon</a>, Alboin made his skull into a drinking cup and married his daughter Rosamund, who later had Alboin murdered.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cunimund.jpg" alt="Cunimund" width="320" height="293" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pietro della Vecchia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pietro_della_Vecchia_-_Rosamund_forced_to_drink_from_the_skull_of_her_father.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
